<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine wheat harvest 71.5 pct completed.</title>
<headline>Argentine wheat harvest 71.5 pct completed.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers harvested 71.5 percent of their 1996/97 wheat crop by Dec 27, the government's Agriculture Secretariat said in its weekly crop report Thursday.</p>
<p>Maize sowing reached 92.0 percent. The maize crop was developing well, benefitting from good rains. Soybean sowing reached 89.3 percent of intentions, helped by recent rain.</p>
<p>Cotton sowing was slowed by continuing rain, especially in Chaco and Formosa provinces. Cotton sowing was 86.6 percent complete. Sunflower sowing was 96.2 percent over. Farmers had planted 88.1 percent of their sorghum.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,983  100.0(100.0)  4,7539   71.5  (76.3)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,765   92.0 (92.5)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,383   89.3 (88.3)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,002   96.2 (98.8)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     760   88.1 (86.4)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	960   86.6  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p>--Buenos Aires Newsroom +541-318-0655</p>
